<comment>
problem = Ambipolar diffusion, VARIABLE eta_A via a localized guide-field Gaussian bump
(iprob=51): B1(x) = Bx*(1+(bump_ratio-1)*exp(-(x/bump_width)^2)); By(x,0) is a SEPARATE
localized Gaussian wave packet amp*exp(-(x/wave_width)^2) (not the global sin/cos of
iprob=50 -- its periodic node/antinode geometry confounds a near/far amplitude comparison).
eta_A=Q_A*B1(x)^2 so the guide-field bump gives a 100x eta_A peak/floor contrast
(bump_ratio=10). SMOOTH case: bump_width=15*dx (comparable to grid scale) -- the regime the
passing uniform-eta unit tests never covered. eint(x) is chosen for exact total-pressure
(thermal+magnetic) equilibrium so B1(x) should stay numerically frozen (ambipolar diffusion
of a purely-x-varying field is analytically null: J3=dBy/dx is the only nonzero current and
dE3/dy=dE2/dz=0) -- tlim is chosen well inside the local AD e-folding time at the bump peak
and well below the bump's sound-crossing time, so any B1 drift signals contamination
(checked post-hoc against the phdf output, not just analytically).
Compare the By(x) profile at tlim against the matched _glm.in run (trusted reference) to
isolate whether CT's edge-EMF averaging under-resolves a diffusivity gradient this sharp.
CT variant (divergence_control=ct); differs from _glm.in ONLY in that line + ct_emf.

<job>
problem_id = diffusion

<problem/diffusion>
iprob       = 51
Bx          = 1.0
amp         = 1.0e-6
bump_ratio  = 10.0
bump_p0     = 200.0
bump_width  = 0.1171875
wave_width  = 0.3515625

<parthenon/mesh>
refinement = none
nghost = 2
nx1 = 128
x1min = -0.5
x1max = 0.5
ix1_bc = periodic
ox1_bc = periodic
nx2 = 8
x2min = -0.03125
x2max = 0.03125
ix2_bc = periodic
ox2_bc = periodic
nx3 = 1
x3min = -0.5
x3max = 0.5
ix3_bc = periodic
ox3_bc = periodic

<parthenon/meshblock>
nx1 = 128
nx2 = 8
nx3 = 1

<parthenon/time>
integrator = vl2
cfl = 0.3
tlim = 2.2e-3
nlim = 10000000
ncycle_out = 200

<hydro>
fluid = glmmhd
riemann = hlld
eos = adiabatic
reconstruction = plm
gamma = 1.6666666666666667
divergence_control = ct
ct_emf = gs05

<diffusion>
integrator = rkl2
cfl = 0.3
rkl2_max_dt_ratio = 400
ambipolar = ambipolar
ambipolar_coeff = fixed
ambipolar_coeff_code = 0.5

<parthenon/output0>
file_type = hdf5
dt = 2.2e-4
variables = prim
id = prim

<parthenon/output1>
file_type = hst
dt = 1.1e-4
